{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/keyboardkit\/developer-custom-keyboards"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]},{"paths":["\/documentation\/keyboardkit\/developer-custom-keyboards"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"occ"}]}],"metadata":{"images":[{"identifier":"Developer-Article-Custom-Keyboards.jpg","type":"card"}],"title":"Custom Keyboard Extensions","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"KeyboardKit"}],"color":{"standardColorIdentifier":"purple"},"roleHeading":"Article"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"This developer guide describes how custom iOS keyboard extensions work."}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit","doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Developer-Articles"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Developer-Data-Syncing","doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Developer-Debugging","doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Developer-dSYMs","doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Developer-Experiments","doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Developer-Memory-Management"],"anchor":"Essentials","generated":true,"title":"Essentials"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Developer-Custom-Keyboards","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/developer.apple.com\/documentation\/uikit\/creating-a-custom-keyboard","type":"reference"},{"text":" is an app extension that you ship together with your app. Once enabled in Settings, it can replace the native system keyboard by selecting it with the bottom-leading 🌐 key while typing.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Keyboard extensions are the only kind of apps that can be used directly with other apps in iOS. By extending your app’s features for use in a custom iOS keyboard, your users will be able to use them in any app that supports text input.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"How-do-I-create-a-custom-keyboard","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"How do I create a custom keyboard?"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You can add a custom keyboard to any iOS app, from Xcode’s “File > New > Target…” menu option. This will add a keyboard extension to your app and make it possible to switch to that keyboard while typing in any app.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"See ","type":"text"},{"overridingTitle":"this article","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/developer.apple.com\/documentation\/uikit\/creating-a-custom-keyboard","overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"this article"}],"type":"reference"},{"text":" for a guide on how to create a custom keyboard extension from scratch, and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/developer.apple.com\/library\/archive\/documentation\/General\/Conceptual\/ExtensibilityPG\/CustomKeyboard.html","type":"reference"},{"text":" for more extensive information.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"What-can-a-custom-keyboard-be-used-for","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"What can a custom keyboard be used for?"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A custom keyboard can be used to provide custom autocomplete & spell-checking functionality, more sophisticated text analysis, AI-based features, etc. The possibilities are endless, but Apple’s native APIs are very limited by default.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"What-can-a-custom-keyboard-do","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"What can a custom keyboard do?"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A custom keyboard can render any user interface and resize the keyboard area to fit its content. It uses a ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"document proxy","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" to read and write text from and to the currnetly active text field, and can require Full Access to enable capabilities like network access.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"What-can-a-custom-keyboard-NOT-do","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"What can a custom keyboard NOT do?"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Apple’s native APIs are very limited, and basically just lets you read and write text in limited ways. Some things are however not possible. For instance, a keyboard can’t draw outside its bounds, and is memory capped at ~70 MB. Apple also doesn’t provide a keyboard view.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Why-should-I-use-KeyboardKit","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Why should I use KeyboardKit?"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"KeyboardKit extends Apple’s native APIs and adds more features to make it a easier to create amazing custom keyboards. KeyboardKit also has a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardView","type":"reference"},{"text":" that renders a native-looking, fully customizable keyboard with just a few lines of code.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Why should I use KeyboardKit Pro?","anchor":"Why-should-I-use-KeyboardKit-Pro","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"KeyboardKit Pro extends KeyboardKit with pro features, like support for 76 locales, autocomplete, dictation, fonts, an emoji keyboard, clipboard management, themes, etc.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Further Reading","anchor":"Further-Reading","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"See ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/developer.apple.com\/documentation\/uikit\/creating-a-custom-keyboard","overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"this article"}],"overridingTitle":"this article","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for a guide on how to create a custom keyboard extension from scratch, and ","type":"text"},{"overridingTitle":"this article","identifier":"https:\/\/developer.apple.com\/library\/archive\/documentation\/General\/Conceptual\/ExtensibilityPG\/CustomKeyboard.html","overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"this article"}],"isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for more extensive information.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"See KeyboardKit’s ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Getting-Started-Article","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" guide for further reading on how KeyboardKit can help you create a custom keyboard from scratch.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit/documentation/KeyboardKit/Developer-Experiments":{"role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"This developer guide describes how to enable experimental features.","type":"text"}],"title":"Experiments","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Developer-Experiments","url":"\/documentation\/keyboardkit\/developer-experiments","type":"topic","kind":"article","images":[{"identifier":"Developer-Article-Experiments.jpg","type":"card"}]},"doc://com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit/documentation/KeyboardKit/Developer-Debugging":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"This developer guide describes how to debug a custom keyboard extension."}],"kind":"article","type":"topic","role":"article","title":"Debugging","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Developer-Debugging","images":[{"identifier":"Developer-Article-Debugging.jpg","type":"card"}],"url":"\/documentation\/keyboardkit\/developer-debugging"},"doc://com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit/documentation/KeyboardKit/Getting-Started-Article":{